      "title": "The benefit period",
      "narration": "The benefit period is how long payments continue for one disability: two years, five years, to age 65 or 67, or for life in older policies. Longer benefit periods cost more. For a career-ending injury the difference between a five-year benefit period and one to age 65 is the whole point of the coverage, so Theo recommends the longer period for Rosa at 41. Benefit periods for sickness and accident may differ. Group plans often define a short-term benefit period in weeks and a long-term period to retirement age, handing off from one to the other.",
