      "title": "Waiver of premium",
      "narration": "Once Rosa has been disabled for a stated period, usually 90 days, the waiver of premium provision excuses her premiums for as long as the disability lasts, and the insurer refunds any premium she paid during those first 90 days. Coverage stays fully in force while she pays nothing. When she recovers, premiums resume. Without the waiver, a disabled insured with no income might let the policy lapse at the moment she needs it most. Most individual disability policies include the waiver automatically; others sell it as a rider.",
