      "title": "Exclusions",
      "narration": "Disability policies exclude losses from war or military service, intentionally self-inflicted injury, participation in a felony, pre-existing conditions during the look-back period, and in nonoccupational policies, injuries covered by workers compensation. Older policies excluded normal pregnancy; modern policies treat pregnancy complications as sickness. Some exclude disability while living outside the country for an extended period or while incarcerated. Put the settings together for Rosa: 3,600 dollars a month, 90-day elimination, benefits to 65, premium waived after 90 days of disability, 24-hour coverage, standard exclusions. That is a complete basic plan.",
